      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's the surprise. All three make the same two products. The gas is hydrogen. The water becomes a solution of the metal hydroxide, which is alkaline, and that's why the indicator turns pink. For sodium, sodium plus water gives sodium hydroxide plus hydrogen. Lithium and potassium do exactly the same, each giving a fizz of hydrogen and a pink solution. So the difference isn't what's made. It's how fast.",
